### The source categories

The right side of the screen is organized into four categories, each one with its own heading:
- **Primary sources**: original documents, objects, and records produced at the time of the events;
- **References**: books, articles, and websites consulted by the team;
- **Religious references**: sacred texts and religious works;
- **Social media**: videos, forums, and other posts shared online.

Each link in the text sends its source to the matching category. Click on the examples below and see where each one appears:
- Primary source: <i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillPrimarySource('0059a36e-b134-4859-bec0-c89e7239d07c'); return false;">INAH. Teotihuacan</a></i>;
- Reference: <i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillReferenceSource('006b21c9-6800-4deb-bb3f-a367dd38b703'); return false;">NOAA (2024). What is longitude?</a></i>;
- Religious reference: <i><a href="#" onclick="htCleanSources(); htFillHolySource('56e19b6d-5b12-4a9d-abff-7c85ff465872'); return false;">Torah (1891)</a></i>;
